<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ecueracapa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1793">1793</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ecueracapa was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comanche">Comanche</a> chief who emerged as the leading spokesman of the western Comanche in the 1780s. In 1786 he negotiated a peace with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-bautista-de-anza">Juan Bautista de Anza</a>, governor of Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-mexico">New Mexico</a>, which ended decades of raiding there and allied the Comanche with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apache">Apache</a>. The peace lasted for decades, and Ecueracapa died in 1793 fighting the Pawnee.</p></div>
